---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { statusLine, tagRows } from "../lib/spec";

const rows = tagRows();
const status = statusLine();
---

<Base title="The obs: tags" description="Every tag of the Open Briefing Standard, one line each." path="/ns">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>The <code>obs:</code> tags</h1>
    <p class="lede">The namespace of the Open Briefing Standard, version 1.</p>
    <pre><code>https://openbriefingstandard.org/ns#</code></pre>
    <p>
      In a page, each tag is a <code>&lt;meta property="obs:…" content="…"&gt;</code> element in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>.
      In an RSS or Atom feed, each is an element in this namespace, declared as
      <code>xmlns:obs="https://openbriefingstandard.org/ns#"</code>. The <a href="/spec/v1">specification</a> is the
      authority; this page is generated from its table.
    </p>
    <p class="note">{status}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap tags">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <tr id={r.name.replace(/:/gu, "-")}>
            <td><code>{r.name}</code></td>
            <td set:html={r.meaning} />
            <td set:html={r.required} />
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>In a feed</h2>
    <p>
      A sub-property becomes an attribute of its parent: <code>obs:summary:short</code> is written
      <code>&lt;obs:summary length="short"&gt;</code>, a highlight's label is <code>&lt;obs:highlight label="…"&gt;</code>, and
      <code>obs:derive:translate</code> and <code>obs:derive:combine</code> are attributes of <code>&lt;obs:derive&gt;</code>.
      <a href="/spec/v1#14-feeds">Section 14</a> has an example.
    </p>
    <h2>Reserved names</h2>
    <p>
      Names under <code>obs:audio:</code>, and <code>obs:highlight:start</code> and <code>obs:highlight:end</code>, are held
      for a later version. A reader ignores them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .tags {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  h1 code {
    font-size: 0.82em;
    padding: 0 0.15em;
  }
</style>
